From df4a10111de2005f9f7ea216343ebe52781a7410 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz Gajoch <gajoch@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:36:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(usb): USB host mode, the default, chosen at boot

The USB-C port can be a USB host, for a hub with a WiFi dongle or an Ethernet
adapter. The board can't supply VBUS; it comes from a powered hub.

- Linux: a usb-host overlay (dr_mode = "host") in kernel.itb, and USB host
  support (DWC2 dual role).
- U-Boot: with usb_mode=host in the env, boot kernel.itb with its usb-host
  configuration on top of the panel one. usb_mode is kept from the saved env.
- S01usb-mode: an unset usb_mode becomes host, so from the second boot after
  an install the port is a host; usb_mode=device keeps it a USB device.
- S30usb-gadget: without a USB device controller, skip the gadget and only
  set the hostname.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
